<title>MALTA: Malta Parliament approves new tax to replace VAT.</title>
<headline>Malta Parliament approves new tax to replace VAT.</headline>
<dateline>VALLETTA 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Maltese Parliament has approved a new system of indirect taxation to replace Value Added Tax.</p>
<p>After a two-day debate, the house where the government has a one-seat majority voted 35-34 for the measure late on Tuesday night. VAT will be replaced on July 1.</p>
<p>The promise to replace VAT is widely seen as having been the most important factor that led to the Labour Party's election to power last October.</p>
